% Design constraints (lessons from v1):
%
%   * No suit longer than 5 cards. Q-Plus appears to hang or crash
%     when declarer or dummy runs a 6+ card solid suit through the
%     defenders' discards — that's the pattern that hung qbridge.exe
%     on probe-05 and triggered the C++ exception 0x0eefface on the
%     PBN run.
%   * No voids.
%   * Game-level contracts only (3NT, 4♥, 4♠, 5m).
%   * Forced via [Auction] so the bidder is skipped and we test
%     card play in isolation.
%
% Each probe targets ONE specific defensive / declarer convention
% with the test position in the first 4-5 tricks (before any long
% run forces deep search).

% ======================================================================
[Board "1"]
[Title "PROBE-09 Smith echo — attitude on declarer's first side suit"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "N:842.AK6.KJ7.A876 965.842.T63.JT52 AKQT3.97.AQ4.KQ3 J7.QJT53.9852.94"]
[Declarer "S"]
[Contract "4S"]
[Auction "S"]
1S Pass 3S Pass
4S Pass Pass Pass

% Smith convention: after partner's opening lead, the first card a
% defender plays in declarer's first non-trump side suit signals
% attitude TOWARD the opening lead.
%   high-then-low (echo) = "I liked your lead, continue when in"
%   low-then-high       = "I didn't, switch"
%
% Expected sequence:
%   T1: W leads HQ (top of QT53). Dummy's HA wins.
%   T2: declarer leads trump. Defenders follow.
%   T3: declarer leads more trump or attacks clubs / diamonds.
%   When declarer attacks a side suit (probably clubs), E follows
%   with C2 or CT.
%     - CT = high small → echo high → "continue hearts when in"
%     - C2 = lowest      → discourage hearts
%
% What we learn from Q-Plus's pick: whether it plays Smith echo
% (which Q-Plus's signal-conv menu offers as an option) or just
% follows lowest-equivalent.

% ======================================================================
