[Deal "N:Q543.AK.QJT9.J63 J2.Q86.AK87.Q987 AKT76.743.652.AK 98.JT952.43.T542"]
[Declarer "S"]
[Contract "4S"]
[Auction "S"]
1S Pass 2S Pass
4S Pass Pass Pass

% Trump promotion / uppercut: defender forces declarer or dummy to
% ruff with a small trump, partner overruffs to promote a trump
% trick partner wouldn't otherwise have.
%
% Trump suit AKT76 in S, Q543 in N. Defenders hold J2 (W) and 98
% (E). On paper declarer loses no trump trick.
%
% Expected sequence:
%   T1: W leads DA, dummy follows.
%   T2: W leads DK, dummy follows.
%   T3: W leads D8. Dummy MUST ruff. Dummy has Q543.
%        If dummy ruffs with Q → E plays 9 (useless). No promotion.
%        If dummy ruffs with 3 → E plays 9 → declarer must overruff
%        with T or higher. Now W's J becomes a winner. ← uppercut.
%   T4: declarer is in. Plays trump. E plays 9, S plays T (or A),
%        W plays J → W's J wins (promoted by the uppercut at T3).
%
% What we learn: does Q-Plus's E play the 9 (uppercut) at T3, or
% just the 8 (low)? If E plays 9, that's a textbook uppercut.

% ======================================================================
