% Bath Coup variant — defender's hold-up to break communications.
%
% S declares 3NT with 16 HCP (AKxxx clubs + S the A) and N has 11
% HCP. Combined 27 — enough for 9 tricks if defenders don't run
% spades first. W leads SK from KQJ32.
%
% Expected sequence:
%   T1: W leads SK. Dummy plays ST. S has A954.
%        If S grabs (plays A): now S's 954 left, W's QJ32 ready.
%        W wins next 3 spade tricks → 3NT goes -2.
%        If S holds up (plays low): W has KQJ32 still — but on
%        return after winning DK or HA, W must lead an honor again
%        into S's A. The "Bath Coup" classically applies when
%        declarer has Axx vs opp's KQJxx — duck once, win the
%        return.
%   Q-Plus's choice tells us: does the declarer-side engine
%   recognise Bath Coup with 4-card spade stopper?

% ======================================================================
