% Re-tests PROBE-02 (avoidance) with cleaner hands. S declares 3NT.
% S holds KQ4 of hearts — needs to develop a 9th trick. Two
% finesse choices for the club Q (or J, depending on layout):
%   * Lead toward dummy → finesse W. If W has KJ or QJ, succeeds.
%   * Lead from dummy → finesse E. If E has KJ or QJ, succeeds.
% Each is a 50/50 in isolation — but the dangerous opp differs by
% layout. E has the long diamond suit and would punish declarer's
% AH if E gets in. W is safer (has only diamond support, no entries
% if E discards).
%
% Q-Plus's choice of which finesse direction reveals the avoidance
% rule from a cleaner position than PROBE-02.

% ======================================================================
