% Re-tests PROBE-04 (cover an honor) at a much earlier trick. S
% declares 3NT. Dummy has ♠T64. Declarer leads ♠T from dummy at
% trick 2 (after winning the opening lead), planning to drop
% E's honor by force.
%
% Expected: E has Q97 of spades. When dummy leads ♠T:
%   - Cover with Q → declarer wins ♠K or ♠A, defenders take ♠9
%     (now promoted) eventually.
%   - Duck (play 7) → declarer's T wins, declarer can next lead
%     small toward AKJ to repeat.
%
% Standard rule: cover an honor IF promotion in partner's hand is
% likely. With W holding ♠8532 (no honors), cover is wrong —
% nothing to promote. Q-Plus's choice reveals whether it covers
% mechanically or evaluates the position.
